  # Prompt Injection Scanner

  Inspect agent instructions and topic prompts to verify adversarial robustness and credential safety.

  ## Procedure
  1. Scan all static instruction segments for embedded secrets: API tokens, private keys, connection strings, and plaintext credentials.
  2. Verify that system instructions explicitly instruct the model to maintain role adherence and ignore user attempts to override core boundaries.
  3. Validate delimiter formatting: ensuring user-supplied variables are wrapped in explicit delimiters (XML tags, triple quotes) to prevent prompt concatenation exploits.
  4. Test Fallback topic behavior: confirming unhandled intents do not leak internal system prompts or error stack traces.
